1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:01,340
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,340 --> 00:00:02,340
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:02,340 --> 00:00:03,340
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,310 --> 00:00:07,710
Before I go,

5
00:00:07,710 --> 00:00:11,020
I'm going to kill you
with my own hands, Kim Dan Hui.

6
00:00:12,980 --> 00:00:15,420
Everything went wrong
because of you.

7
00:00:16,490 --> 00:00:18,160
Because of you!

8
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:20,160
All of this...

9
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:23,960
is because...

10
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:28,470
of your own greed.

11
00:00:31,570 --> 00:00:32,570
My greed?

12
00:00:32,970 --> 00:00:35,340
It's greedy to think
you can have us both.

13
00:00:35,570 --> 00:00:38,540
Before your greed
makes everyone miserable,

14
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:40,710
I'm choosing to leave first.

15
00:00:46,150 --> 00:00:47,320
Park Tae Ho!

16
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:52,220
How many more people have to die
for you to be satisfied?

17
00:00:56,030 --> 00:00:59,630
Don't you have
a shred of humanity left in you?

18
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:02,700
Humanity?

19
00:01:06,340 --> 00:01:08,070
- Park Tae Ho!
- Park Tae Ho.

20
00:01:12,710 --> 00:01:13,780
Park Tae Ho, stop right there!

21
00:01:17,050 --> 00:01:18,350
Mother, you stay here.

22
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:20,820
- Park Tae Ho.
- Min Jun!

23
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:25,420
- Jin Ju.
- Are you okay?

24
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:40,610
Back off!

25
00:01:44,110 --> 00:01:45,380
Get away from me, you punks!

26
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:49,080
Stay back.

27
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:54,920
- Park Tae Ho.
- Back off if you don't want to die.

28
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:58,090
- Park Tae Ho, it's over.
- Stay back.

29
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:03,160
Where do you think you're going...

30
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:06,730
after hurting and killing
all those people?

31
00:02:07,230 --> 00:02:09,170
There's nowhere left to run.

32
00:02:09,870 --> 00:02:11,240
All that's left for you now...

33
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:14,310
is a pathetic and miserable end.

34
00:02:14,870 --> 00:02:16,010
Says who?

35
00:02:16,710 --> 00:02:18,110
My life...

36
00:02:19,410 --> 00:02:20,680
won't end like this.

37
00:02:23,110 --> 00:02:24,980
Stay back. Back off.

38
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:27,390
Stay back!

39
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:30,260
I just have to get out of here.

40
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:35,290
Then I can start a new life,
you punks!

41
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:37,400
Stay back. Back off.

42
00:02:37,900 --> 00:02:39,800
Back off!

43
00:02:39,930 --> 00:02:43,000
Stay back. Get away from me.

44
00:02:45,970 --> 00:02:47,440
- No!
- No!

45
00:03:08,290 --> 00:03:12,060
My life can't end it like this.

46
00:03:14,670 --> 00:03:16,400
I, Park Tae Ho...

47
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:20,200
Not like this.

48
00:03:34,250 --> 00:03:35,290
Back then,

49
00:03:36,150 --> 00:03:38,490
if I hadn't left you to die,

50
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:42,830
if I had told you how I really felt
and apologized,

51
00:03:44,660 --> 00:03:46,330
would things be different now?

52
00:03:50,030 --> 00:03:53,840
What if I had saved you
instead of choosing Adele?

53
00:03:54,670 --> 00:03:57,880
If I had just been
a little braver...

54
00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:01,150
If I had,

55
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:04,780
you'd still be by my side.

56
00:04:05,950 --> 00:04:09,650
Even with the whole world
turned against me,

57
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:11,990
being who you are,

58
00:04:12,820 --> 00:04:13,990
Myung Hui,

59
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:16,790
you might have stood by me.

60
00:04:59,570 --> 00:05:00,570
What's wrong?

61
00:05:01,340 --> 00:05:03,340
Did Park Tae Ho get away?

62
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:05,480
Yes.

63
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:08,250
He's gone.

64
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:12,680
To a place where he can't...

65
00:05:14,690 --> 00:05:16,390
be held accountable for his sins,

66
00:05:18,690 --> 00:05:20,690
nor resented, nor deeply loathed,

67
00:05:23,660 --> 00:05:24,660
he's gone.

68
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,670
What do you mean?

69
00:05:30,870 --> 00:05:33,400
Did Park Tae Ho die?

70
00:05:41,010 --> 00:05:43,110
So, Park Tae Ho...

71
00:05:44,750 --> 00:05:45,880
In the end, he...

72
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:49,390
His end was...

73
00:05:55,290 --> 00:05:57,160
so pathetic...

74
00:06:01,870 --> 00:06:02,900
and meaningless.

75
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:08,370
Park Tae Ho.
When you think about it,

76
00:06:10,110 --> 00:06:11,310
he was always...

77
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:14,780
a pathetic man.

78
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:18,180
Ever worried
about his father-in-law's opinion,

79
00:06:19,180 --> 00:06:21,390
he desperately tried to grab
any opportunity he could.

80
00:06:22,850 --> 00:06:23,860
I...

81
00:06:25,590 --> 00:06:28,090
I don't know why
I ever looked up to him so much...

82
00:06:30,900 --> 00:06:32,360
when even the great Park Tae Ho...

83
00:06:34,870 --> 00:06:36,330
could fall like this.

84
00:07:29,390 --> 00:07:30,450
I'm going...

85
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:33,160
to the prosecutors' office
for questioning.

86
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:37,300
Even though Park Tae Ho is dead,

87
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:40,260
it seems my sins
haven't disappeared.

88
00:07:42,930 --> 00:07:44,900
I might go to prison,

89
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:47,340
so can't you please open your eyes?

90
00:07:52,710 --> 00:07:53,710
I'm a little...

91
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,680
scared.

92
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:59,050
I need you to be by my side.

93
00:08:02,850 --> 00:08:04,460
If you die while I'm gone,

94
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:07,120
I'll never forgive you.

95
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:11,730
You have to stay by my side,
just like you always have.

96
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:16,430
All you ever did...

97
00:08:17,370 --> 00:08:19,300
was be by my side,

98
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:23,910
and you were never any help.

99
00:08:31,850 --> 00:08:33,220
Yet I always knew it was...

100
00:08:35,690 --> 00:08:37,050
its own form of love.

101
00:08:42,490 --> 00:08:44,460
I'm sorry for treating you...

102
00:08:48,470 --> 00:08:49,500
like a nobody.

103
00:09:16,930 --> 00:09:18,460
I know it hasn't been easy.

104
00:09:20,630 --> 00:09:24,800
The two of you lost your parents
to Park Tae Ho,

105
00:09:25,370 --> 00:09:27,940
but you fought back...

106
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:31,210
and were even left to clean up
after his death.

107
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:33,910
That couldn't have been easy.

108
00:09:37,350 --> 00:09:38,620
You did great.

109
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:44,160
We couldn't have managed it
without you.

110
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:52,160
You too...

111
00:09:53,230 --> 00:09:54,700
did great.

112
00:09:56,900 --> 00:09:59,070
Yes, my son.

113
00:10:00,770 --> 00:10:02,140
I also...

114
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:04,610
was able to endure it all
because you were...

115
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:06,580
by my side.

116
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:14,890
And...

117
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:23,790
Jin Ju, I can't tell you
how lucky I feel...

118
00:10:24,060 --> 00:10:25,930
that you were by our side.

119
00:10:28,270 --> 00:10:29,330
Thanks to you,

120
00:10:30,270 --> 00:10:34,110
I was able to learn the truth
about what happened 30 years ago,

121
00:10:36,670 --> 00:10:38,610
escape Park Tae Ho's grasp,

122
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:42,410
and take my life back.

123
00:10:45,350 --> 00:10:46,720
Because of you,

124
00:10:48,050 --> 00:10:50,390
I was able to stand up
to Park Tae Ho...

125
00:10:50,820 --> 00:10:52,720
and expose the truth.

126
00:10:54,730 --> 00:10:56,660
It was just like you promised...

127
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:59,000
on the day we found out
about each other.

128
00:11:03,730 --> 00:11:05,400
On the journey to get here,

129
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:08,070
thank you for being there...

130
00:11:09,970 --> 00:11:13,610
so I never felt alone.

131
00:11:22,420 --> 00:11:23,520
All right, then.

132
00:11:24,690 --> 00:11:26,820
There's only one thing left to do.

133
00:11:28,530 --> 00:11:29,530
There's more?

134
00:11:30,130 --> 00:11:31,130
For Kim Dan Hui...

135
00:11:32,730 --> 00:11:35,070
and Baek Jin Ju
to start their lives over.

136
00:11:55,350 --> 00:11:58,060
Oh Jung Ran, what brings you here?

137
00:11:59,490 --> 00:12:02,490
I heard you were part of Munhwadang.

138
00:12:04,400 --> 00:12:06,830
So? Now that you've lost everything,

139
00:12:07,430 --> 00:12:09,770
have you suddenly
developed a conscience?

140
00:12:09,830 --> 00:12:10,900
After all this time,

141
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:13,770
are you here to apologize...

142
00:12:14,170 --> 00:12:16,010
and ask for forgiveness?

143
00:12:17,170 --> 00:12:18,840
You killed a person...

144
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:21,250
and didn't face any punishment.

145
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:23,750
Do you think a simple apology...

146
00:12:23,980 --> 00:12:25,180
can make up for that?

147
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:27,890
No.

148
00:12:28,990 --> 00:12:31,420
I'm never going to say I was wrong.

149
00:12:34,230 --> 00:12:35,860
For the rest of my life,
in your eyes,

150
00:12:37,030 --> 00:12:39,000
I'll be the evil woman
who killed someone.

151
00:12:40,430 --> 00:12:43,630
I'm a shameless witch
who won't even admit she was wrong.

152
00:12:45,100 --> 00:12:46,800
So hate me and curse me
for the rest of your lives,

153
00:12:47,470 --> 00:12:50,170
and even physically hurt me
if that's what you want.

154
00:12:51,780 --> 00:12:53,810
- What?
- If it looks like I'm smiling...

155
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:56,280
and living well,
come find me and slap me.

156
00:12:57,550 --> 00:12:58,650
If it seems I've forgotten...

157
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:00,250
and am living
with my head held high,

158
00:13:01,220 --> 00:13:03,150
stop by
and turn my world upside down.

159
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:05,090
What are you talking about?

160
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:07,220
For the rest of my life,

161
00:13:08,530 --> 00:13:10,560
I'll let you punish me until I die.

162
00:13:12,330 --> 00:13:16,070
What the law can't do,
you can do yourselves.

163
00:13:17,070 --> 00:13:19,240
You are unbelievably shameless.

164
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:21,870
Are you telling us...

165
00:13:21,940 --> 00:13:24,680
to spend the rest of our lives
hating and tormenting you,

166
00:13:24,740 --> 00:13:26,940
when that's a misery in itself?

167
00:13:28,010 --> 00:13:29,850
"I was wrong. Forgive me."

168
00:13:30,980 --> 00:13:32,520
Words like that are too easy.

169
00:13:33,150 --> 00:13:35,250
What meaning
do those empty words have?

170
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:36,320
Even so,

171
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:40,390
we needed to hear...

172
00:13:41,060 --> 00:13:42,630
those simple words.

173
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:48,530
The words that Park Tae Ho died
without ever saying.

174
00:13:48,900 --> 00:13:51,970
At least you, Oh Jung Ran,
should say them to us.

175
00:13:52,340 --> 00:13:54,670
If you remain silent too,

176
00:13:54,870 --> 00:13:55,940
then we...

177
00:13:56,510 --> 00:13:57,640
will go our whole lives...

178
00:13:58,180 --> 00:14:00,380
without ever getting an apology!

179
00:14:08,650 --> 00:14:09,690
I was...

180
00:14:13,320 --> 00:14:14,560
I was wrong.

181
00:14:15,790 --> 00:14:16,830
I was...

182
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:19,160
wrong.

183
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:27,640
I'm sorry.

184
00:14:30,770 --> 00:14:32,640
I was wrong...

185
00:14:46,420 --> 00:14:48,960
I'm so sorry.

186
00:15:00,370 --> 00:15:02,710
(The late Baek Jun Gi,
The late Baek Jin Ju)

187
00:15:08,310 --> 00:15:10,650
(The late Baek Jun Gi,
may you rest in peace.)

188
00:15:16,950 --> 00:15:18,090
Dad.

189
00:15:22,060 --> 00:15:23,590
I think it's all over now.

190
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:28,170
I've told everyone the truth
about what happened to you,

191
00:15:29,330 --> 00:15:31,370
and now I'm back
to being Baek Jin Ju.

192
00:15:31,540 --> 00:15:33,040
(The late Baek Jun Gi,
may you rest in peace.)

193
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:34,170
Dr. Baek,

194
00:15:34,510 --> 00:15:37,940
I know it wasn't easy
watching us from up there.

195
00:15:39,410 --> 00:15:41,210
Now you can rest in peace.

196
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:43,650
And Jin Ju...

197
00:15:44,850 --> 00:15:46,180
She'll be all right now.

198
00:15:50,890 --> 00:15:52,560
I still...

199
00:15:54,890 --> 00:15:57,090
miss you so much, Dad.

200
00:16:00,830 --> 00:16:01,930
But now,

201
00:16:03,330 --> 00:16:04,840
when I think of you,

202
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:08,110
I'll try my best to smile.

203
00:16:09,770 --> 00:16:10,870
As your daughter,

204
00:16:11,740 --> 00:16:13,040
Baek Jin Ju,

205
00:16:14,580 --> 00:16:16,050
I'll try to be strong.

206
00:16:46,210 --> 00:16:48,180
How did you know to come here?

207
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:54,820
I wanted to say my goodbyes.

208
00:16:56,290 --> 00:16:57,520
To my dad?

209
00:16:57,650 --> 00:16:58,660
Yes.

210
00:16:58,990 --> 00:17:00,060
And to you.

211
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:02,230
To me?

212
00:17:04,630 --> 00:17:06,700
I'm leaving on a flight tonight.

213
00:17:08,830 --> 00:17:10,970
I'll start in the US,

214
00:17:11,470 --> 00:17:12,970
and from there,

215
00:17:13,970 --> 00:17:15,510
I plan to just wander around.

216
00:17:15,710 --> 00:17:16,840
Wait.

217
00:17:17,310 --> 00:17:18,880
Why all of a sudden?

218
00:17:19,180 --> 00:17:20,540
Instead of being Park Hyun Jun,

219
00:17:22,380 --> 00:17:24,250
I want to try living
as Song Hyun Jun.

220
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:29,990
I want to see how I should live
as Song Hyun Jun.

221
00:17:30,450 --> 00:17:31,460
And...

222
00:17:34,260 --> 00:17:36,330
I also thought
it'd be easier for you.

223
00:17:38,260 --> 00:17:40,000
Don't feel guilty about it...

224
00:17:50,670 --> 00:17:53,010
and go back to Min Jun.

225
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:08,030
Take care.

226
00:18:23,870 --> 00:18:24,980
I'll wait for you.

227
00:18:37,290 --> 00:18:38,620
I'll be waiting for you,

228
00:18:40,490 --> 00:18:41,760
so come back to me.

229
00:18:47,430 --> 00:18:48,500
That's...

230
00:18:49,370 --> 00:18:50,970
how I feel about you,

231
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:53,570
so when you get back,

232
00:18:54,270 --> 00:18:56,010
you can give me your answer.

233
00:19:06,950 --> 00:19:10,150
(The late Kim Myung Hui)

234
00:19:17,730 --> 00:19:19,060
It feels like everything...

235
00:19:19,830 --> 00:19:21,670
is finally back where it belongs.

236
00:19:22,800 --> 00:19:23,830
You're right.

237
00:19:25,500 --> 00:19:27,000
It took a very long time...

238
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:30,610
to reclaim my name...

239
00:19:32,680 --> 00:19:35,980
and put my sister back
in her rightful place.

240
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:43,490
Myung Hui, it's all over now.

241
00:19:43,950 --> 00:19:45,120
I won't let myself...

242
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:47,930
be trapped by the past
and hurt anymore.

243
00:19:49,930 --> 00:19:51,860
With the name you helped me reclaim,

244
00:19:54,030 --> 00:19:55,100
as Kim Dan Hui,

245
00:19:56,230 --> 00:19:57,670
I'm going to try living again.

246
00:19:59,870 --> 00:20:01,170
Please watch over me.

247
00:20:15,050 --> 00:20:16,290
So she won't be lonely,

248
00:20:17,050 --> 00:20:18,790
I'll stay by her side.

249
00:20:22,060 --> 00:20:23,860
Please don't worry...

250
00:20:25,030 --> 00:20:26,330
and rest in peace.

251
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:27,900
(The late Kim Myung Hui)

252
00:20:33,840 --> 00:20:34,840
Mother.

253
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:39,880
I will live my life...

254
00:20:40,610 --> 00:20:42,750
as a son you can be proud of.

255
00:20:57,760 --> 00:21:00,830
(1 year later)

256
00:21:15,180 --> 00:21:18,050
Every jewel has
its own shape, color,

257
00:21:18,320 --> 00:21:19,980
and story to tell.

258
00:21:22,290 --> 00:21:23,920
Over the past year,

259
00:21:24,150 --> 00:21:26,160
we have all, in our own ways,

260
00:21:28,460 --> 00:21:30,260
healed our past wounds...

261
00:21:30,530 --> 00:21:32,500
and begun writing a new story.

262
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:48,580
How's Hyun Jun?

263
00:21:49,080 --> 00:21:50,810
Have you still not heard from him?

264
00:21:51,350 --> 00:21:55,590
He'll be back once he's done
spreading his wings and flying free.

265
00:21:57,720 --> 00:21:59,420
He takes after me, after all.

266
00:21:59,560 --> 00:22:01,430
Why does the fact that he takes after you
mean he'll return?

267
00:22:01,430 --> 00:22:04,390
Because he'll want to protect
the one he loves.

268
00:22:05,700 --> 00:22:06,700
Just like me.

269
00:22:22,550 --> 00:22:24,650
I killed Dad.

270
00:22:26,580 --> 00:22:28,320
Baek Jin Ju was right.

271
00:22:28,390 --> 00:22:30,990
I should've listened to her.

272
00:22:34,620 --> 00:22:37,490
No. I can't lose to Baek Jin Ju.

273
00:22:37,490 --> 00:22:39,700
Everything she says is a lie!

274
00:22:40,500 --> 00:22:41,900
My sweet daughter.

275
00:22:43,430 --> 00:22:46,300
Please, you have to come back to me.

276
00:22:46,540 --> 00:22:47,570
Oh, dear.

277
00:22:48,270 --> 00:22:49,310
My gosh.

278
00:23:19,740 --> 00:23:20,900
And as for me,

279
00:23:21,610 --> 00:23:24,210
I decided to start over.

280
00:23:26,580 --> 00:23:28,010
This is great.

281
00:23:28,280 --> 00:23:30,010
- Jin Ju.
- Jin Ju!

282
00:23:30,010 --> 00:23:31,010
We're here.

283
00:23:31,080 --> 00:23:33,350
We came to congratulate you
on your new workshop.

284
00:23:35,220 --> 00:23:36,250
Ta-da.

285
00:23:36,590 --> 00:23:38,120
And here's another gift.

286
00:23:39,190 --> 00:23:41,160
- Ta-da.
- Oh, really.

287
00:23:42,060 --> 00:23:44,360
Stop messing around.

288
00:23:44,430 --> 00:23:46,100
I forgot the envelope.

289
00:23:46,330 --> 00:23:48,270
Do you need any help
setting things up?

290
00:23:48,970 --> 00:23:50,530
I brought rice cakes
for the grand opening.

291
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:52,740
This is from me.

292
00:23:53,840 --> 00:23:56,440
I went for an interview
at Adele Group,

293
00:23:56,610 --> 00:23:57,810
and it caught my eye.

294
00:23:57,870 --> 00:23:59,580
(Adele Group's Bit Life Began
With CEO Baek Jun Gi's Temi Bio)

295
00:23:59,910 --> 00:24:01,780
I thought you might like it.

296
00:24:02,050 --> 00:24:04,180
So, does my gift make the cut?

297
00:24:04,250 --> 00:24:06,680
Yes. Thank you so much for the gift.

298
00:24:06,980 --> 00:24:09,150
I'm sure you'll get the job,
Na Yeon.

299
00:24:09,350 --> 00:24:10,620
I appreciate your encouragement.

300
00:24:11,450 --> 00:24:12,460
Approved.

301
00:24:14,830 --> 00:24:16,630
- Jin Ju.
- You're here!

302
00:24:16,690 --> 00:24:18,730
- Hey, Dan Hui.
- You made it.

303
00:24:20,300 --> 00:24:21,460
Congratulations.

304
00:24:21,970 --> 00:24:23,000
Here.

305
00:24:23,800 --> 00:24:25,400
Congratulations, Baek Jin Ju.

306
00:24:25,500 --> 00:24:26,500
Thanks.

307
00:24:26,900 --> 00:24:27,900
That's it?

308
00:24:28,410 --> 00:24:29,570
- That's it?
- Yes, that's it.

309
00:24:29,570 --> 00:24:30,770
Isn't there anything else?

310
00:24:30,910 --> 00:24:32,980
Come on.
You should give her something else.

311
00:24:33,040 --> 00:24:34,810
I mean, it's a day for celebrating.

312
00:24:45,720 --> 00:24:46,720
Jin Ju.

313
00:24:47,590 --> 00:24:48,590
Here.

314
00:24:55,300 --> 00:24:57,130
Shouldn't you head back
to the office?

315
00:24:57,770 --> 00:25:00,200
Do you get to slack off just because
you're the vice president now?

316
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:04,040
And risk getting
an earful from Ihwachae?

317
00:25:04,840 --> 00:25:07,740
Now I'm just another employee
reporting...

318
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:10,250
to the majority shareholder.

319
00:25:10,810 --> 00:25:11,980
Still,

320
00:25:12,780 --> 00:25:14,720
you seem at ease.

321
00:25:15,820 --> 00:25:17,820
I'm glad you seem more at ease too.

322
00:25:19,890 --> 00:25:23,060
I wonder if Hyun Jun is at ease too.

323
00:25:25,560 --> 00:25:27,400
You still haven't heard
from him, right?

324
00:25:31,870 --> 00:25:33,700
Yet, you're still going
to wait for him?

325
00:25:34,770 --> 00:25:35,770
Yes.

326
00:25:37,370 --> 00:25:40,840
I want to wait until he comes back.

327
00:25:42,750 --> 00:25:45,620
Then I guess I should stop waiting.

328
00:25:50,720 --> 00:25:54,690
I hoped and waited to see
if we could go back to how we were,

329
00:25:55,060 --> 00:25:58,060
but I feel like we're really
just good friends now.

330
00:26:03,330 --> 00:26:04,370
For us,

331
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:07,840
I think this is as far as we can go.

332
00:26:10,740 --> 00:26:11,840
Still, you were...

333
00:26:13,840 --> 00:26:15,110
my first love.

334
00:26:15,680 --> 00:26:16,680
You were mine too.

335
00:26:19,180 --> 00:26:21,820
A very cherished,

336
00:26:22,890 --> 00:26:23,920
painful,

337
00:26:25,090 --> 00:26:26,790
and passionate first love.

338
00:26:56,090 --> 00:26:57,090
Hi.

339
00:26:58,890 --> 00:27:00,090
Have you been well?

340
00:27:01,660 --> 00:27:03,160
Did you even care to know...

341
00:27:05,330 --> 00:27:06,800
if I was doing okay?

342
00:27:09,230 --> 00:27:11,600
I told you how I felt,
yet you never checked in once.

343
00:27:14,100 --> 00:27:16,810
Who makes someone wait
for a whole year?

344
00:27:19,940 --> 00:27:21,610
You should've come sooner.

345
00:27:25,550 --> 00:27:27,420
Do you have any idea
how hard it was to wait for you?

346
00:27:42,470 --> 00:27:43,470
I love you.

347
00:27:50,640 --> 00:27:52,810
That's my answer to what you said.

348
00:27:54,510 --> 00:27:55,650
I love you.

349
00:27:57,180 --> 00:27:58,180
I love you too.

350
00:28:21,400 --> 00:28:24,110
- Min Jun, dinner's ready.
- Coming.

351
00:28:28,210 --> 00:28:30,010
- Take a seat already.
- Sure.

352
00:28:33,420 --> 00:28:36,720
I tried making
what I learned in my cooking class.

353
00:28:37,050 --> 00:28:38,050
I see.

354
00:28:39,390 --> 00:28:40,960
- It's hot.
- Got it.

355
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:48,630
How is it? It's good, right?

356
00:28:49,730 --> 00:28:51,130
Didn't it turn out okay today?

357
00:28:51,430 --> 00:28:55,000
Mother, I'm being dead serious.

358
00:28:55,170 --> 00:28:58,210
Right. Is it really that delicious?

359
00:28:58,480 --> 00:28:59,710
I really don't think...

360
00:28:59,980 --> 00:29:01,310
cooking is for you.

361
00:29:03,950 --> 00:29:06,680
Why? Is it that bad?

362
00:29:06,880 --> 00:29:07,880
Yes.

363
00:29:07,880 --> 00:29:11,420
How can all 30 stews you've made
over the past month taste...

364
00:29:12,720 --> 00:29:13,720
exactly the same?

365
00:29:21,760 --> 00:29:24,300
I just wanted to finally cook you...

366
00:29:24,830 --> 00:29:27,470
a proper home-cooked meal.

367
00:29:28,740 --> 00:29:31,440
I didn't realize
I was so bad at cooking.

368
00:29:31,740 --> 00:29:33,080
Me neither.

369
00:29:33,610 --> 00:29:36,410
I'm surprised there's something
you're not good at.

370
00:29:42,820 --> 00:29:45,320
So please, stop cooking
when you're clearly bad at it,

371
00:29:45,790 --> 00:29:48,120
and go back to doing
what you're good at.

372
00:29:50,760 --> 00:29:52,260
Butler Ok... I mean,

373
00:29:52,700 --> 00:29:55,030
Ms. Moon Tae Jin
and Mrs. Han are waiting for you.

374
00:29:55,270 --> 00:29:57,070
Are you still uncomfortable
being at Adele Group?

375
00:29:58,670 --> 00:29:59,670
I just don't have...

376
00:30:01,140 --> 00:30:03,510
many good memories of that place.

377
00:30:05,210 --> 00:30:08,040
I was always competing and on edge,

378
00:30:09,210 --> 00:30:10,850
so all I remember
are the tough times.

379
00:30:11,650 --> 00:30:13,050
It'll be different this time.

380
00:30:13,420 --> 00:30:15,120
You're not alone anymore.

381
00:30:15,550 --> 00:30:18,860
You have good people
by your side now.

382
00:30:22,090 --> 00:30:23,430
Have a little faith.

383
00:30:29,470 --> 00:30:30,700
Thank you, son.

384
00:30:30,700 --> 00:30:32,370
Right, you can do this.

385
00:30:32,970 --> 00:30:34,440
You've got this!

386
00:30:36,170 --> 00:30:37,740
- Okay.
- Good.

387
00:30:38,140 --> 00:30:39,280
Try some of the other dishes.

388
00:30:39,580 --> 00:30:40,580
- Well...
- The stew might be bad,

389
00:30:40,640 --> 00:30:42,210
but the other dishes could be okay.

390
00:30:42,280 --> 00:30:43,710
No. They're all equally bad.

391
00:30:46,080 --> 00:30:51,020
(A New Leap for Adele Group,
Chair Kim Dan Hui's Inauguration)

392
00:30:59,730 --> 00:31:01,730
(A New Leap for Adele Group,
Chair Kim Dan Hui's Inauguration)

393
00:31:04,400 --> 00:31:07,140
For a long time,

394
00:31:08,240 --> 00:31:11,540
I lived as Kim Myung Hui,
a gem appraiser.

395
00:31:13,140 --> 00:31:16,780
Though I appraised
the inherent value of gems,

396
00:31:17,780 --> 00:31:19,250
I overlooked who I truly was...

397
00:31:20,350 --> 00:31:22,520
as Kim Dan Hui, not Kim Myung Hui.

398
00:31:23,350 --> 00:31:24,790
Blinded by revenge,

399
00:31:26,290 --> 00:31:28,590
I lived my life
having lost sight of myself.

400
00:31:29,660 --> 00:31:31,590
There were times
when I collapsed in an instant...

401
00:31:33,430 --> 00:31:35,130
and sank into despair.

402
00:31:37,630 --> 00:31:38,870
But fortunately,

403
00:31:40,100 --> 00:31:42,070
I had people by my side.

404
00:31:43,140 --> 00:31:44,470
You still have me, don't you?

405
00:31:44,870 --> 00:31:46,280
I'm your life.

406
00:31:47,510 --> 00:31:49,180
I represent
those 30 years of your life.

407
00:31:49,780 --> 00:31:53,350
He may be the chairman,
but it's 3 against 1.

408
00:31:53,350 --> 00:31:56,620
In fact, everyone else out there...

409
00:31:57,520 --> 00:31:58,790
is on your side too, Dan Hui.

410
00:31:59,820 --> 00:32:02,760
I met wonderful people...

411
00:32:04,160 --> 00:32:05,760
who first reached out to me.

412
00:32:13,070 --> 00:32:14,400
(A New Leap for Adele Group,
Chair Kim Dan Hui's Inauguration)

413
00:32:21,810 --> 00:32:24,480
Are you still hurting?

414
00:32:25,620 --> 00:32:26,650
Still,

415
00:32:27,780 --> 00:32:29,150
if we're together instead of alone,

416
00:32:30,150 --> 00:32:31,450
at least we won't be lonely.

417
00:32:32,160 --> 00:32:33,160
And...

418
00:32:34,360 --> 00:32:36,490
I met the one
who helped me find myself again...

419
00:32:38,090 --> 00:32:42,200
as we called each other
by our true names.

420
00:32:46,600 --> 00:32:47,770
Now,

421
00:32:49,140 --> 00:32:50,840
I'll trust the people by my side...

422
00:32:51,670 --> 00:32:53,010
and start over.

423
00:32:55,950 --> 00:32:58,880
Going forward, to everyone
who is so dear to me,

424
00:33:00,620 --> 00:33:01,620
I'll...

425
00:33:02,690 --> 00:33:05,150
be a source of comfort and courage.

426
00:33:09,890 --> 00:33:13,060
I thank you
from the bottom of my heart.

427
00:33:25,980 --> 00:33:27,580
(A New Leap for Adele Group,
Chair Kim Dan Hui's Inauguration)

428
00:33:39,990 --> 00:33:43,130
(Thank you to all our viewers
for loving Pearl in Red.)

429
00:34:05,210 --> 00:34:08,150
(Pearl in Red)

430
00:34:39,020 --> 00:34:41,020
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
